| Detection Metadata                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Detection Name    : Lateral Movement via SMB Admin Shares                             |
| Detection ID      : DET-007                                                           |
| MITRE Tactic      : Lateral Movement                                                  |
| MITRE Technique   : T1021.002 — SMB/Windows Admin Shares                             |
| Severity          : High                                                              |
| Data Sources      : WinEvent 4624 (Logon Type 3), WinEvent 5140 (Share Access)       |

================================================================================
PRIMARY QUERY — Admin Share Access Detection
================================================================================

index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security"
EventID=5140
(ShareName="*ADMIN$*" OR ShareName="*C$*" OR ShareName="*IPC$*")
NOT IpAddress IN ("127.0.0.1","::1","192.168.10.10","192.168.10.30")
| eval detection="Admin Share Access — Possible Lateral Movement"
| eval mitre="T1021.002"
| eval severity="High"
| eval risk_level=if(
    ShareName="*ADMIN$*" OR ShareName="*C$*",
    "HIGH — administrative share accessed",
    "MEDIUM — IPC$ access, possible recon"
  )
| table _time, ComputerName, Account_Name, IpAddress, ShareName, ObjectType, risk_level
| sort -_time

================================================================================
SECONDARY QUERY — Network Logon + Admin Share Correlation
================================================================================

index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security"
(EventID=4624 Logon_Type=3) OR (EventID=5140)
| transaction Account_Name maxspan=2m
| where eventcount > 1
| eval detection="Network Logon + Share Access — Lateral Movement Pattern"
| table _time, Account_Name, ComputerName, eventcount
| sort -_time

================================================================================
KNOWN FALSE POSITIVES
================================================================================
- IT admin remote management (RMM tools, PSExec for legitimate use)
- Backup software accessing shares (exclude known backup server IPs)
- File server access from known admin workstations
